    "lines": [
      {
        "scene": "hook",
        "text": "Worth billions, and his salary is a single dollar? Why?",
        "start": 0.27,
        "seconds": 2.15,
        "window": 2.57,
        "fill": 0.837
      },
      {
        "scene": "promise",
        "text": "Three levels explain it, and the last one is where the billions quietly grow, year after year.",
        "start": 2.83,
        "seconds": 3.78,
        "window": 4.33,
        "fill": 0.873
      },
      {
        "scene": "salary",
        "text": "The normal way is a salary. Say $50,000,000 a year. At an assumed top rate of 37%, the tax takes $18.5M first. He keeps $31.5M.",
        "start": 7.17,
        "seconds": 9.15,
        "window": 9.73,
        "fill": 0.94
      },
      {
        "scene": "shares",
        "text": "But he already owns shares worth $50,000,000. In 5 years, at an assumed 7%, those shares are worth $70.1M.",
        "start": 16.9,
        "seconds": 6.68,
        "window": 6.83,
        "fill": 0.978
      },
      {
        "scene": "decade",
        "text": "Give it 10 years: $98.4M. And the tax on all that growth? Nothing, as long as he never sells.",
        "start": 23.73,
        "seconds": 5.45,
        "window": 6.0,
        "fill": 0.908
      },
      {
        "scene": "paycheck",
        "text": "Hang on. My paycheck gets taxed every single month, and I don't own a company to grow instead!",
        "start": 29.73,
        "seconds": 3.63,
        "window": 3.9,
        "fill": 0.931
      },
      {
        "scene": "turn",
        "text": "Exactly. A salary is taxed the day it's paid. Shares are taxed only when they're sold.",
        "start": 33.63,
        "seconds": 3.57,
        "window": 4.1,
        "fill": 0.871
      },
      {
        "scene": "payoff",
        "text": "So the tiny salary isn't kindness. His real pay is $48.4M of growth, and none of it is taxed until he sells.",
        "start": 37.73,
        "seconds": 6.13,
        "window": 6.67,
        "fill": 0.919
      },
